---
layout: base
---
{% from "macros/section-bar.njk" import sectionBar %}
{% set pageSubtitle = subtitle or (navigation.items | getDescription(page.url)) %}

{#
    The list-shaped index pages are headed by a section bar, then the page's
    own line and any facts about the list beside it in the margin. The line
    is the page's Directory description, read from the navigation data so
    the two cannot describe the page differently; a page without an entry
    there (a topic) gives its own `description`. `listFacts` is an array of
    { label, value } pairs set in the page's data, such as the bookshelf's
    total. Prose pages keep the title and subtitle treatment.
#}
<article class="page">
    {%- if listPage %}
    {{ sectionBar(title, 1) }}
    {%- set listIntro = (navigation.items | getDescription(page.url)) or description %}
    {%- if listIntro or listFacts %}
    <div class="list-header margin-grid">
        {%- if listIntro %}
        <p class="list-intro">{{ listIntro }}</p>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if listFacts %}
        <dl class="facts">
            {%- for fact in listFacts %}
            <div class="facts__item"><dt>{{ fact.label }}</dt><dd>{{ fact.value }}</dd></div>
            {%- endfor %}
        </dl>
        {%- endif %}
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- else %}
    {#
        A prose page takes the post's header: title and subtitle in the main
        column, its facts in the margin beside the title. A page dates itself
        only when it opts in with `showUpdated`, because on most pages here
        the fact is noise: a colophon is not truer for having been edited
        last week.

        `lastUpdated` wins over `page.date` where it is given. `page.date`
        is git's last-modified, which moves whenever any commit touches the
        file, so a typo fix or a site-wide restyle restamps a page whose
        content has not changed in a year. The sitemap prefers the same
        field for the same reason.
    #}
    <header class="page-header post-header">
        <h1 class="page-title">{{ title }}</h1>
        {% if pageSubtitle %}
        <p class="page-subtitle">{{ pageSubtitle }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        {%- if showUpdated %}
        {%- set updated = lastUpdated or page.date %}
        <dl class="facts">
            <div class="facts__item facts__item--labelled"><dt>Updated</dt><dd><time datetime="{{ updated | w3Date }}">{{ updated | htmlDate }}</time></dd></div>
        </dl>
        {%- endif %}
    </header>
    {%- endif %}
    <div class="page-content">
        {{ content | safe }}
    </div>
</article>
